  "_key": "!scenes!2c6ea531f81cb6ce",
  "description": "<p>The building where Euphoria lives. <strong>Four Lone Star officers</strong> respond to the PANICBUTTON within five minutes; the alarm can be cancelled inside five minutes with a memorised code.</p><p>The desk guard keeps a loaded <strong>Enfield AS7 shotgun</strong> behind the desk. The courier on duty will not fight — average human, all 3s.</p><p>Elevators are thumbprint-locked and auto-select the resident's floor; bypassing needs an Electronics (5) Test, base time five minutes.</p><p><strong>Rooms:</strong> Front entrance and guard station (four sets of double doors, computer terminal, PANICBUTTON alarm, camera, visitor-verification speaker), bar, private meeting room, lecture room doubling as a small theatre, store, garden courtyard, storeroom, men's and women's restrooms with sauna and shower, pool. Three elevators.</p><p><em>Layout derived from the printed floorplan on Queen Euphoria p.14. Measured 26 × 21 m by grid period 42 px/m on a 200 dpi render of book p.14; wall runs isolated by ink thickness. Wall-to-wall footprint measures 25.8 x 20.8 m, so the scene is 26 x 21 with a 0.5 m margin. The previous 27 x 20 came from a coarser 31 px/m read. — the map carries a \"□ = 1 metre\" legend, so the scale is the book's, not an estimate.</em></p>"
}
